WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.926
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.678
[man] <i>Hey!</i>

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

4
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.155
Bean. it's really you.

5
00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:33.659
Yes. Mom. it's... it's me. I grew.

6
00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:35.202
Mostly my teeth.

7
00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:37.996
You... You were turned to stone.

8
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.708
My God! And you freed me? Bean. I...

9
00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:44.211
[crying]

10
00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.672
I... I can't believe you're back.

11
00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:48.590
This is all so crazy.

12
00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:52.636
[stammers] I can't really believe
that you're alive and Elfo is dead.

13
00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.138
I had to choose between...

14
00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.641
I had to choose you. [sighs]

15
00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:01.645
Oh. there. there. Don't cry. darling.
Mommy's here now.

16
00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:04.898
Wow. I feel better already.

17
00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:06.233
What do you call this?

18
00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:07.734
Affection.

19
00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:17.911
Hey. Who goes there?

20
00:01:17.995 --> 00:01:21.498
[Bean] Princess Tiabeanie
and Queen Dagmar!

21
00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:23.333
Oi. you havin' a bit of a laugh?

22
00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:27.129
Princess Bean is always drunk
at this hour. and you ain't even slurring!

23
00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:29.423
And Queen Dagmar? [laughs]

24
00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:31.049
She's been dead for years.

25
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:35.345
No. but I haven't eaten in over a decade.
so hurry up and open the gate.

26
00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:37.681
[gasps] Your Majesty...

27
00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.349
[screams]

28
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:43.770
I deserve this fate for doubting you!

29
00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:59.077
Ah. that unforgettable stench
of manure and boiling cabbage.

30
00:01:59.161 --> 00:02:00.162
There's cabbage?

31
00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.833
[shrieks] The ghost of Queen Dagmar!

32
00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:06.543
Is it really you?

33
00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:09.963
Bunty. Still adorably dim. I see.

34
00:02:10.047 --> 00:02:12.215
Dim as the day is long. Your Majesty.

35
00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:14.343
Stop poking the royal tit. dear.

36
00:02:14.426 --> 00:02:16.428
[indistinct chatter]

37
00:02:17.012 --> 00:02:18.889
Sorcerio. Odval.

38
00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.183
I can't believe my eyes.

39
00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:26.104
Dad! Dad! You're not gonna believe this!
Open up!

40
00:02:26.188 --> 00:02:28.231
[groaning] Come on...

41
00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:32.110
Whoa! Holy mother of Bean.

42
00:02:32.194 --> 00:02:33.695
Is it really you?

43
00:02:33.779 --> 00:02:35.697
Why don't you kiss me and find out?

44
00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:36.823
Whoa.

45
00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:43.914
I've been dreaming of this moment
for 15 years.

46
00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.750
Look at you.
You haven't changed a bit.

47
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.335
[chuckles]

48
00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:50.712
And you. You've only got bigger...

49
00:02:50.796 --> 00:02:52.547
[stammers] Better.

50
00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:53.715
[chuckles]

51
00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:58.178
I was so sad about losin' ya.
I turned to food for solace.

52
00:02:58.261 --> 00:02:59.638
But you're back!

53
00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:01.515
Let's throw a huge feast!

54
00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:03.642
I don't need
all that attention. sweetheart.

55
00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:06.311
I'll arrange for something
small and tasteful.

56
00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:08.397
[crowd cheering and applauding]

57
00:03:10.399 --> 00:03:11.983
[crowd] Dagmar!

58
00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:20.117
Incredible.

59
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.829
All that malarkey with the magic elf blood
actually paid off.

60
00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:26.581
It took all season. but it did.

61
00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:30.585
And by season. I mean fall or summer.
or whatever this is.

62
00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:32.379
[herald] Hear ye. hear ye!

63
00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:36.049
Returning to the court
for the first time in 15 years.

64
00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:42.139
once a statue. now statuesque.
it's the dagmarvelous Dagmar!

65
00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.641
[all cheering and applauding]

66
00:03:44.725 --> 00:03:46.560
The long wait is over.

67
00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:48.937
Your wonderful queen has arrived.

68
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.857
Aw. aren't you sweet. darling?

69
00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.442
[all gasp]

70
00:03:53.525 --> 00:03:56.153
Thank you for your kind gasps.

71
00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.779
It's wonderful to... [gasps]

72
00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:02.409
Uh. ladies. it's gonna be okay.

73
00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:05.120
Odval. explain how it's gonna be okay.

74
00:04:05.203 --> 00:04:07.706
I'll begin with an introduction.

75
00:04:07.789 --> 00:04:11.668
Queen Oona of Dreamland.
meet Queen Dagmar...

76
00:04:11.752 --> 00:04:13.587
Also of Dreamland.

77
00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.630
The cotton candy shop called.

78
00:04:15.714 --> 00:04:17.215
They want their hair back.

79
00:04:18.008 --> 00:04:19.092
[door closes]

80
00:04:19.176 --> 00:04:22.804
Really. I only married her
to get the canal built.

81
00:04:22.888 --> 00:04:24.014
How practical.

82
00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.974
Yeah. real practical.

83
00:04:26.057 --> 00:04:29.770
She also gave me a son. so now.
I finally got an heir to the throne!

84
00:04:29.853 --> 00:04:31.229
Also practical.

85
00:04:31.313 --> 00:04:35.442
And you allowed that amphibian
to raise my precious Tiabeanie?

86
00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:38.320
No. no. no.
I was mostly raised by Bunty.

87
00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:40.280
And a bunch of friendly drunks
down at the pub.

88
00:04:40.363 --> 00:04:42.449
They taught me the fine art of stabbing.

89
00:04:42.532 --> 00:04:45.368
Believe me. I kept her
on the straight and narrow.

90
00:04:45.452 --> 00:04:46.995
Uh. when I had time.

91
00:04:47.078 --> 00:04:49.289
Dad tried for years
to find the Elixir of Life.

92
00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:51.458
We searched the entire world.

93
00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:53.919
Good men died to bring you back. baby.

94
00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:56.588
Yeah. like Elfo. my best friend.

95
00:04:56.671 --> 00:05:00.342
Aw. that sweet. poor little bastard
with the funny head.

96
00:05:00.425 --> 00:05:01.468
I'm gonna miss him.

97
00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:04.888
Sounds to me like he deserves
a marvelous funeral.

98
00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.014
Great idea.

99
00:05:06.097 --> 00:05:08.600
I'll get someone to fish him
out of the corpse pit.

100
00:05:08.683 --> 00:05:10.268
[bell tolling]

101
00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:16.233
[bagpipes playing

102
00:05:31.957 --> 00:05:35.001
You know. I'm gonna miss that Elfo.

103
00:05:35.085 --> 00:05:37.546
He watered my plants while I was in rehab.

104
00:05:40.131 --> 00:05:40.966
[honk]

105
00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:47.806
Hey. Tess. what happened to your eye?

106
00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.558
Oh. I had to stop using the eye.

107
00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:52.269
It's just too painful
seeing the truth all the time.

108
00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:55.272
Ah. that's why humans tend to avoid it.

109
00:05:59.651 --> 00:06:01.695
The procession left without me.

110
00:06:01.778 --> 00:06:03.697
Oh. that's too bad.

111
00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:06.616
I blame myself
'cause I didn't even notice.

112
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.703
The queen's place
is at the side of the king.

113
00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:13.415
Oh. Queen Oona. Of course.
This is terribly awkward.

114
00:06:13.498 --> 00:06:17.294
Please. take my spot.
I'll find another place to sit.

115
00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:19.421
Mmm. that's better.

116
00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:23.758
Yeah. sure. Both of yas with me.

117
00:06:23.842 --> 00:06:25.886
Plenty of Zog to go around.

118
00:06:26.845 --> 00:06:29.014
Beanie. make with the eulogy already.

119
00:06:29.598 --> 00:06:31.433
[sighs] Okay. here we go.

120
00:06:31.516 --> 00:06:35.604
Elfo and I had only been friends
for a few months.

121
00:06:35.687 --> 00:06:38.565
but they really were
the best months of my life.

122
00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:40.567
Even though much of his time was spent

123
00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.236
as the subject
of barbaric medical experiments...

124
00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:45.155
She's talking about me.

125
00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:47.908
...he changed the way I looked at things.

126
00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:53.121
In a kingdom of talking cats
and enchanted pigs and hooker fairies.

127
00:06:53.204 --> 00:06:55.832
Elfo grounded me in reality.

128
00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:59.419
I'm really. really going to miss him.

129
00:07:05.008 --> 00:07:06.551
Rest in peace. buddy.

130
00:07:06.635 --> 00:07:09.054
Sorry they had to bury you
in this aquarium.

131
00:07:16.603 --> 00:07:20.315
[grunts] After the king goes the queen!

132
00:07:20.398 --> 00:07:23.735
Sorry. Queen Oona.
I didn't mean to ruffle your feathers.

133
00:07:23.818 --> 00:07:28.657
For the last time. they are not feathers.
I am not bird-type!

134
00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:30.241
[crowd gasps]

135
00:07:30.325 --> 00:07:32.118
You will respect me!

136
00:07:32.202 --> 00:07:35.163
You are not the queen.
You are reanimated corpse!

137
00:07:35.246 --> 00:07:37.082
How dare you!

138
00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:41.294
[both grunt]

139
00:07:41.962 --> 00:07:45.131
[all] Queen fight! Queen fight!
Queen fight!

140
00:07:45.215 --> 00:07:47.217
Your Highness. do something.

141
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.427
Ladies. ladies! Come on!

142
00:07:49.511 --> 00:07:51.846
I'm much more embarrassed
than I am aroused.

143
00:07:58.561 --> 00:08:00.021
[all gasp]

144
00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:14.411
Elfo! No!

145
00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.621
There. there. He's with the crabs now.

146
00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.546
Mom! Oh. my God. are you okay?

147
00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:27.465
You know what. Oona? You're insane!

148
00:08:27.549 --> 00:08:29.217
Why don't you just get out of here?

149
00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.260
[Oona growls]

150
00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:40.186
Ha! I foresee trouble
in someone's future.

151
00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:42.564
You're going to have to choose. sire.

152
00:08:42.647 --> 00:08:44.858
You can't have two queens.

153
00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:48.611
[groans] I can't just tell
one of 'em to get lost.

154
00:08:48.695 --> 00:08:50.655
Dagmar is the love of my life.

155
00:08:50.739 --> 00:08:54.784
And Queen Oona is the mother of Derek.
the heir to the throne.

156
00:08:54.868 --> 00:08:58.121
Oh. nonetheless. she is quite unpopular
in the kingdom.

157
00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:01.624
We've gotten dozens of complaints
about her late-night howling.

158
00:09:01.708 --> 00:09:05.045
If we disgrace Oona.
it could mean war with Dankmire.

159
00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:07.964
Queen Oona has outlived her usefulness.

160
00:09:08.048 --> 00:09:12.302
I don't think anyone would care
if she were to vanish.

161
00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:15.055
[hisses]

162
00:09:15.138 --> 00:09:18.099
We will see who is going to vanish.

163
00:09:21.728 --> 00:09:26.983
I had Odval clear my schedule.
so we got the whole night to ourselves.

164
00:09:27.067 --> 00:09:28.902
Oh. darling. So ambitious.

165
00:09:29.903 --> 00:09:32.447
[Luci] Excuse me. Pardon me.
Cat with a ball.

166
00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.324
Bean. you poor baby!

167
00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:36.618
What a horrific day you've had.

168
00:09:36.701 --> 00:09:39.329
Let's have too much wine
and forget about it all.

169
00:09:39.412 --> 00:09:42.373
Hey. I thought we were gonna have wine
and forget stuff.

170
00:09:42.457 --> 00:09:43.917
Dad. come on!

171
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.836
This is my first chance
to have a conversation with a parent

172
00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.005
without half of it being muttered
under their breath.

173
00:09:49.089 --> 00:09:52.050
[mutters] What is this. some kinda
slam against me? Well. okay.

174
00:09:52.133 --> 00:09:53.176
[Luci grunts]

175
00:09:53.802 --> 00:09:56.304
Kick me out... Why. I oughta...
[continues muttering]

176
00:09:58.932 --> 00:10:02.185
I can't believe
I'm reduced to talking to you.

177
00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:04.896
Hey. the feeling is mutual.
but here we are.

178
00:10:04.979 --> 00:10:07.148
So. how did you... Oona!

179
00:10:07.232 --> 00:10:10.110
Hey. sweetie. wait! Let's talk. [panting]

180
00:10:12.362 --> 00:10:16.366
Damn. Well. it's gonna be
another long. lonely night.

181
00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:18.034
Good night. Vip. Good night. Vap.

182
00:10:20.578 --> 00:10:23.039
[screams] Don't sneak up on a guy...

183
00:10:23.123 --> 00:10:25.250
Oh. wait. [chuckles]
Nothing to be scared of.

184
00:10:25.333 --> 00:10:28.962
Ooh. silly me.
It's just a statue of Pendergast...

185
00:10:29.045 --> 00:10:30.797
that I've never seen before.

186
00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.759
Sculpted in a bizarre
and unlikely pose. Huh.

187
00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.222
Oh. well. Who can say
what passes for art these days? [chuckles]

188
00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:44.018
I had them make brunch for us.

189
00:10:44.102 --> 00:10:48.815
All your favorites: poached dodo eggs.
unicorn bacon and waffles.

190
00:10:48.898 --> 00:10:51.442
How thoughtful.
but Bean and I are going riding.

191
00:10:51.526 --> 00:10:54.779
Okay. Be safe. darling. [kisses]

192
00:10:58.032 --> 00:11:00.160
Wub you. snuggums!

193
00:11:01.452 --> 00:11:04.038
Ugh. have some dignity. man.

194
00:11:04.122 --> 00:11:06.749
You're the king.
not some lovelorn old fool.

195
00:11:06.833 --> 00:11:08.251
How did you get like this?

196
00:11:08.334 --> 00:11:09.711
You really wanna know?

197
00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:13.590
Then pour a drink. light a cigar
and hand 'em both to me.

198
00:11:14.465 --> 00:11:17.760
<i>I was known as Zog the Warrior Prince.</i>

199
00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:20.805
Had enough?

200
00:11:20.889 --> 00:11:23.183
Uh. yup. I'm good. [groans]

201
00:11:23.683 --> 00:11:27.145
[Zog] <i>My older brother Yog.
who'd been next in line for the throne.</i>

202
00:11:27.228 --> 00:11:29.355
<i>- was mysteriously poisoned.</i>
- [choking]

203
00:11:29.439 --> 00:11:33.943
[Zog] <i>So the crown was mine.
but I was no ruler. I was a fighter.</i>

204
00:11:34.027 --> 00:11:36.613
<i>Fighting. competing. winning.</i>

205
00:11:36.696 --> 00:11:38.573
<i>That was all I wanted to do...</i>

206
00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.410
[crowd cheering and applauding]

207
00:11:42.493 --> 00:11:44.996
[Zog] <i>...until I laid eyes on her.</i>

208
00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.877
<i>A noble's daughter from a far-off land.</i>

209
00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.796
<i>and she was all I'd ever wanted.</i>

210
00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:56.132
<i>Our life together was perfect.</i>

211
00:11:56.216 --> 00:11:57.884
<i>and it only got perfecter</i>

212
00:11:57.967 --> 00:12:00.428
<i>- when our one and only child came along.</i>
- [Bean babbles]

213
00:12:00.511 --> 00:12:02.722
She's got her father's nose.

214
00:12:02.805 --> 00:12:04.140
Nice grip.

215
00:12:04.224 --> 00:12:06.893
[Zog] <i>But then came that fateful night.</i>

216
00:12:06.976 --> 00:12:10.563
<i>After my brother was poisoned.
I'd been so careful.</i>

217
00:12:10.647 --> 00:12:15.902
<i>but as time went on.
I was so happy. I just sorta forgot.</i>

218
00:12:15.985 --> 00:12:17.987
I'm afraid the taster is late. sire.

219
00:12:18.071 --> 00:12:19.989
but I've brought up a bottle
from the cellar.

220
00:12:20.073 --> 00:12:21.658
The seal is unbroken.

221
00:12:29.499 --> 00:12:32.794
No. no. Beanie. That's not for you.
[chuckles]

222
00:12:32.877 --> 00:12:35.964
God knows. as my daughter.
you'll have plenty when you're older.

223
00:12:36.589 --> 00:12:38.258
Come. Zoggy. Make a toast.

224
00:12:38.341 --> 00:12:39.342
Gwapes!

225
00:12:44.222 --> 00:12:46.140
To our little family.

226
00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.688
No! Oh. no!

227
00:12:51.771 --> 00:12:55.858
- Please. not her. No!
- [Dagmar] Bean?

228
00:12:55.942 --> 00:12:58.111
<i>The poison had been meant for me.</i>

229
00:12:58.194 --> 00:13:01.322
<i>but because Bean
had switched the glasses. I lived.</i>

230
00:13:01.406 --> 00:13:04.909
<i>and my beloved Dagmar was turned to stone.</i>

231
00:13:04.993 --> 00:13:07.662
Now. I poured my heart out to you.

232
00:13:07.745 --> 00:13:10.790
You tell me. how'd you get to be
a talking cat?

233
00:13:10.873 --> 00:13:15.044
You keep shoveling waffles in your mouth
while I think of an answer. [vocalizing]

234
00:13:19.632 --> 00:13:23.052
This is where I come to clear my head.
or to sleep it off.

235
00:13:23.136 --> 00:13:26.389
[sighs] I can't believe
it's hardly changed at all.

236
00:13:26.472 --> 00:13:27.473
You know this place?

237
00:13:27.557 --> 00:13:30.518
I used to come here
when I needed a minute for myself.

238
00:13:30.601 --> 00:13:33.313
Your father. bless him.
but his voice does carry.

239
00:13:33.396 --> 00:13:35.857
How cool that we both come up here!

240
00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:37.650
Tell me something else that you like.

241
00:13:37.734 --> 00:13:41.237
- Well. I love the smell of wet grass.
- Me. too!

242
00:13:41.321 --> 00:13:43.323
Oh. how funny. We're so alike!

243
00:13:43.406 --> 00:13:45.408
All right. favorite food on three.

244
00:13:45.491 --> 00:13:47.368
One. two. three.

245
00:13:47.452 --> 00:13:48.453
- Beer!
- Beer!

246
00:13:48.536 --> 00:13:51.247
- Oh. my baby. Are you thirsty?
- Always.

247
00:13:51.331 --> 00:13:52.540
Off to the pub.

248
00:13:59.422 --> 00:14:01.257
I fear my days are numbered.

249
00:14:01.341 --> 00:14:04.844
We will send a message to Dankmire.
of the utmost urgency.

250
00:14:09.223 --> 00:14:10.516
[turkey clucking]

251
00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:14.437
Not a word of this to anyone.
The royal family would not approve.

252
00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:15.897
Bah! To hell with them!

253
00:14:16.522 --> 00:14:20.526
Zog will pay. Dagmar will pay!
Tiabeanie will pay!

254
00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:22.653
They will all pay!

255
00:14:23.154 --> 00:14:25.156
I have to warn the princess.

256
00:14:30.036 --> 00:14:33.289
Oh. come on. Martin. you twit. Aim!

257
00:14:33.373 --> 00:14:35.333
I love how you already know everyone.

258
00:14:35.416 --> 00:14:37.377
It's almost like you were never away.

259
00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:38.795
Almost.

260
00:14:38.878 --> 00:14:40.588
I'm sorry I wasn't here for you. Bean.

261
00:14:40.671 --> 00:14:42.840
I know you've had some difficult years.

262
00:14:42.924 --> 00:14:44.384
Bad shot. mate!

263
00:14:44.467 --> 00:14:46.177
I'm sure your father tried.

264
00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.595
He got my best friend killed.

265
00:14:47.678 --> 00:14:49.972
Yes. well. I said "tried."

266
00:14:50.056 --> 00:14:52.475
Throw the bloody thing. Wayne!

267
00:14:52.558 --> 00:14:53.976
As I was saying.

268
00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:57.397
your father did all he could.
but a girl just needs her mother.

269
00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.314
I know.

270
00:14:58.398 --> 00:15:00.983
Man. you have no idea
how much I've missed you.

271
00:15:01.067 --> 00:15:03.528
I am so glad to have you back.

272
00:15:03.611 --> 00:15:06.114
And I'm not going anywhere
without you. Bean.

273
00:15:06.197 --> 00:15:07.365
Remember that.

274
00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.131
[slurring] Hey. hey. Bunty.
can you steer my stumbles

275
00:15:23.214 --> 00:15:24.382
in the direction of the bed?

276
00:15:24.465 --> 00:15:26.592
I just need... Is... I know...

277
00:15:26.676 --> 00:15:30.263
All right. I know you're still in shock
that my mom is back.

278
00:15:30.346 --> 00:15:33.766
I'm in shock. too. I mean. it is shocking.

279
00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.726
It is shocking.

280
00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:37.770
But. hey. hey. hey. Bunts...

281
00:15:37.854 --> 00:15:43.067
Here's the thing.
Here's the positive thing here.

282
00:15:43.151 --> 00:15:45.027
is you won't have to do as much

283
00:15:45.111 --> 00:15:47.363
'cause she'll be here
to hold my hair back and stuff.

284
00:15:47.447 --> 00:15:49.240
You know? You know what I mean?

285
00:15:49.866 --> 00:15:50.700
Bunts?

286
00:15:51.701 --> 00:15:52.869
What are you doing?

287
00:15:54.245 --> 00:15:55.538
[gasps]

288
00:15:55.621 --> 00:15:57.748
Oh. man. Oh. man!

289
00:15:57.832 --> 00:15:59.750
You gotta help me! Please!

290
00:15:59.834 --> 00:16:02.378
Bunty has been turned to stone.
and I just...

291
00:16:02.462 --> 00:16:04.172
Oh. no. Oh. no. no. no. no. no.

292
00:16:04.255 --> 00:16:05.298
[gasps]

293
00:16:08.885 --> 00:16:11.179
[screaming]

294
00:16:13.097 --> 00:16:15.808
We have to do something. Now!

295
00:16:15.892 --> 00:16:17.643
Any one of us could be next.

296
00:16:17.727 --> 00:16:20.271
Women aren't permitted
to address the council.

297
00:16:20.354 --> 00:16:22.231
But you're the only one in here!

298
00:16:22.315 --> 00:16:23.566
Then it's unanimous.

299
00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:25.234
Shut up. will ya?

300
00:16:25.318 --> 00:16:28.738
Ah. I should've done something earlier.
but now. I got no choice.

301
00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:30.490
I have to take action.

302
00:16:30.573 --> 00:16:31.866
I hate action!

303
00:16:31.949 --> 00:16:33.576
But against whom. sire?

304
00:16:33.659 --> 00:16:34.911
It's gotta be Oona.

305
00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:38.289
She's finally snapped
after years of us being dicks to her.

306
00:16:38.372 --> 00:16:40.082
Any attack against Queen Oona

307
00:16:40.166 --> 00:16:42.877
would be seen as an act of war
on Dankmire.

308
00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.255
A war you'd have to fight
with most of your cabinet turned to stone.

309
00:16:46.339 --> 00:16:49.050
Zog was the greatest warrior
Dreamland has ever seen.

310
00:16:49.133 --> 00:16:51.260
You dare question his fitness for battle?

311
00:16:51.344 --> 00:16:52.303
Not at all.

312
00:16:52.386 --> 00:16:55.431
Only the wisdom of proceeding
without a strategy for...

313
00:16:55.515 --> 00:16:56.933
My clothes are really heavy.

314
00:16:57.016 --> 00:16:59.602
Can we have this conversation
sitting down?

315
00:16:59.685 --> 00:17:02.355
[sighs] You know what? Never mind.

316
00:17:02.438 --> 00:17:05.233
Zoggy. you have to.
Before she comes after one of us.

317
00:17:05.316 --> 00:17:08.611
We can't let our family
be ripped apart again.

318
00:17:12.114 --> 00:17:13.741
[Derek] "More tea. General?"

319
00:17:13.824 --> 00:17:15.743
"Why. certainly. my good man."

320
00:17:17.203 --> 00:17:20.706
Father! To what do I owe
the pleasure of this visit?

321
00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.917
So. listen. son.

322
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:27.213
Your mother and I.
we've been having some. um...

323
00:17:27.296 --> 00:17:28.965
difficulties lately.

324
00:17:29.048 --> 00:17:32.760
and I'd like to lock you in the tower
until we sort things out.

325
00:17:32.843 --> 00:17:35.388
All right. But you'll come get me later?

326
00:17:35.471 --> 00:17:39.642
Sure. Once we work things out.
whoever survives will come and get you.

327
00:17:39.725 --> 00:17:43.646
Okay. but I'm still having nightmares
about that big skillet.

328
00:17:44.146 --> 00:17:46.190
We couldn't find Oona anywhere. sire.

329
00:17:46.274 --> 00:17:48.776
I'm afraid we made the mistake
of trusting her.

330
00:17:48.859 --> 00:17:51.445
She could get any of us at any moment.

331
00:17:51.529 --> 00:17:53.406
We gotta split up and search for her.

332
00:17:53.489 --> 00:17:55.700
Hmm. I have a better idea.

333
00:17:56.325 --> 00:17:58.869
Go ahead. sire.
Don't ask about my fourth eye!

334
00:17:59.495 --> 00:18:03.916
Almighty ball. is Oona still in Dreamland?

335
00:18:05.167 --> 00:18:06.919
- "Yes."
- [all gasp]

336
00:18:07.003 --> 00:18:09.380
Wait. its answers are often cryptic.

337
00:18:09.463 --> 00:18:11.841
Is Queen Oona in the castle?

338
00:18:12.758 --> 00:18:14.802
"The danger is near."

339
00:18:15.303 --> 00:18:16.262
Let me try.

340
00:18:16.345 --> 00:18:17.680
Where is...

341
00:18:17.763 --> 00:18:19.015
[screams]

342
00:18:19.098 --> 00:18:21.100
Enough! No more time for parlor tricks.

343
00:18:21.183 --> 00:18:23.603
We've got to protect ourselves.
I'll watch Bean.

344
00:18:23.686 --> 00:18:25.271
And we'll track down Oona.

345
00:18:25.354 --> 00:18:29.650
I'll use my skills as a hunter
and Odval will use his diplomacy

346
00:18:29.734 --> 00:18:31.736
to stab her with a broom handle.

347
00:18:36.949 --> 00:18:39.410
Follow me. darling.
We'll be completely safe up here.

348
00:18:39.994 --> 00:18:42.830
Wow. Does Dad even know about this room?

349
00:18:42.913 --> 00:18:44.665
No. It's called the library.

350
00:18:51.797 --> 00:18:54.675
Huh. So. what was going on here?

351
00:18:55.926 --> 00:18:57.011
Neat trick.

352
00:18:58.262 --> 00:18:59.388
Then what happened?

353
00:18:59.972 --> 00:19:01.182
[tape rewinds]

354
00:19:02.099 --> 00:19:04.852
<i>Let me try. Where is...</i>

355
00:19:04.935 --> 00:19:06.020
[screams]

356
00:19:06.103 --> 00:19:07.355
Whoa.

357
00:19:07.438 --> 00:19:09.607
Can we try running it back
a little further?

358
00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.276
Actually. a lot further?

359
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.444
[tape rewinds]

360
00:19:21.786 --> 00:19:24.664
You can rest easy now
and get some fresh air.

361
00:19:24.747 --> 00:19:26.749
I used to spend many nights up here.

362
00:19:26.832 --> 00:19:29.502
watching the stars. the moon.
the neighbors.

363
00:19:29.585 --> 00:19:32.922
Mom? That's never happened before.
the thing with my fingers...

364
00:19:33.005 --> 00:19:36.342
As you reach maturity.
you will notice many more changes.

365
00:19:36.425 --> 00:19:39.095
Duh. I already know.

366
00:19:39.178 --> 00:19:40.596
This isn't a sex talk.

367
00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.683
Oh. What kind of talk is it?

368
00:19:43.766 --> 00:19:46.936
There are some things you need to know
about yourself. Bean.

369
00:20:10.418 --> 00:20:11.252
Oh. my!

370
00:20:16.674 --> 00:20:18.718
[Zog] The old castle mental ward.

371
00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:22.555
[Odval] Someone left the door open.

372
00:20:26.183 --> 00:20:27.643
- Hey.
- [both scream]

373
00:20:28.227 --> 00:20:31.272
Oona. is that you?
I missed you so much. baby.

374
00:20:31.355 --> 00:20:32.815
Quick. Odval. stab her in the neck!

375
00:20:32.898 --> 00:20:34.692
[chuckles] Calm down.

376
00:20:35.359 --> 00:20:37.862
I've got something real for you
to freak out about.

377
00:20:38.863 --> 00:20:42.324
Dude. the truth has been
right under your nose the whole time.

378
00:20:42.408 --> 00:20:43.993
but you were too in love to see it.

379
00:20:44.076 --> 00:20:45.453
Show us what happened here.

380
00:20:45.995 --> 00:20:48.372
Okay. now let's take it back
about 15 years.

381
00:20:48.456 --> 00:20:49.457
[tape rewinds]

382
00:20:56.422 --> 00:20:58.174
<i>To our little family.</i>

383
00:21:03.804 --> 00:21:05.097
<i>No! Oh. no!</i>

384
00:21:05.181 --> 00:21:08.642
<i>- Please. not her. No!</i>
- [Dagmar]<i> Bean?</i>

385
00:21:09.143 --> 00:21:10.186
Incredible.

386
00:21:10.269 --> 00:21:12.229
It's exactly as I remembered it.

387
00:21:12.313 --> 00:21:15.274
Except. this time. watch from over here.

388
00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:16.901
[tape rewinds]

389
00:21:17.943 --> 00:21:19.820
<i>...but I've brought up a bottle
from the cellar.</i>

390
00:21:19.904 --> 00:21:21.655
<i>The seal is unbroken.</i>

391
00:21:31.415 --> 00:21:32.416
Dagmar?

392
00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:34.460
She poisoned the wine?

393
00:21:34.543 --> 00:21:38.005
But if Bean hadn't switched
the glasses around. I'd be...

394
00:21:38.088 --> 00:21:41.926
Uh-huh. Out there in the garden
with pigeons crapping on your head.

395
00:21:42.009 --> 00:21:43.010
More so than usual.

396
00:21:43.093 --> 00:21:45.971
But I devoted my life to her. I...

397
00:21:46.972 --> 00:21:48.265
How could she?

398
00:21:48.349 --> 00:21:51.727
Looks like she's been keeping
quite a few secrets from you. my man.

399
00:21:51.811 --> 00:21:54.730
[Zog] What the...
A movable knickknack nook?

400
00:21:54.814 --> 00:21:56.065
[growls]

401
00:21:56.148 --> 00:21:59.944
The thing about your father. Tiabeanie.
is that he wants to change you.

402
00:22:00.027 --> 00:22:02.530
I want you as you were born to be.

403
00:22:02.613 --> 00:22:05.658
What was I born to be? Mom?

404
00:22:05.741 --> 00:22:09.328
Damn small print.
This had better be the right one.

405
00:22:09.411 --> 00:22:11.705
[door opens]

406
00:22:12.665 --> 00:22:13.499
Oh!

407
00:22:21.882 --> 00:22:22.842
[Zog] You.

408
00:22:22.925 --> 00:22:25.386
The only woman I ever loved.

409
00:22:25.469 --> 00:22:29.598
Do you know what I did for you?
What I gave up to get you back?

410
00:22:32.893 --> 00:22:36.939
[sighs] Elfo. I just wish I could see you
one last time.

411
00:22:38.232 --> 00:22:39.191
[panting]

412
00:22:39.275 --> 00:22:44.280
You know. we could've just gone
to marriage counseling.

413
00:22:44.363 --> 00:22:46.282
This goes way beyond you and me. dear.

414
00:22:46.365 --> 00:22:49.952
It is a dark battle of a hundred centuries
and our daughter's destiny.

415
00:22:50.035 --> 00:22:51.745
Not if I can help it.

416
00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:54.123
[Zog grunting]

417
00:22:55.666 --> 00:22:56.584
Come on!

418
00:23:18.564 --> 00:23:21.191
Huh? What is that? Goo?

419
00:23:24.361 --> 00:23:25.195
Yikes!

420
00:23:28.949 --> 00:23:31.994
Summon the army!
This kingdom is under attack!

421
00:23:32.077 --> 00:23:36.999
By a ruthless enemy
who will stop at nothing. My wife!

422
00:23:37.082 --> 00:23:40.794
- [soldier] Which one?
- I do know how to pick 'em. don't I?

423
00:23:43.589 --> 00:23:46.508
[Dagmar] We must go. darling. Quickly.
The attack has begun.

424
00:23:46.592 --> 00:23:48.093
What? Whose attack?

425
00:23:48.177 --> 00:23:52.097
I'm afraid it's Oona.
She is coming for us. For you.

426
00:23:52.181 --> 00:23:53.349
For me?

427
00:23:53.432 --> 00:23:56.769
You. and you alone. are the key
to the future of this kingdom.

428
00:23:56.852 --> 00:23:58.270
All you need is my guidance.

429
00:23:59.021 --> 00:24:00.022
Really?

430
00:24:01.273 --> 00:24:03.442
Sire. we've rallied the troops.

431
00:24:03.525 --> 00:24:05.694
Get out. Run! Save yourself.

432
00:24:05.778 --> 00:24:06.612
From what?

433
00:24:06.695 --> 00:24:08.864
[all screaming]

434
00:24:12.284 --> 00:24:13.160
[man] Oh. no.

435
00:24:13.452 --> 00:24:15.287
I should be the one killing everyone.

436
00:24:15.371 --> 00:24:17.164
I should be the one creeping everyone out.

437
00:24:17.247 --> 00:24:19.041
[gasps] You!

438
00:24:19.124 --> 00:24:19.959
- [Luci yelps]
- [pop]

439
00:24:21.627 --> 00:24:23.629
[all screaming]

440
00:24:30.844 --> 00:24:34.473
[stammering] Wait. this is...
this is just... It's a lot.

441
00:24:34.556 --> 00:24:36.684
I know. sweetie. This way.

442
00:24:36.767 --> 00:24:40.145
What did you mean when you said.
"The future of this kingdom"?

443
00:24:40.229 --> 00:24:42.564
Are you saying I'm some kind of hero?

444
00:24:42.648 --> 00:24:45.526
They're such relative terms.
aren't they. darling?

445
00:24:45.609 --> 00:24:48.112
Hero and villain? One step up.

446
00:24:48.195 --> 00:24:50.155
- I didn't say "villain."
- [Dagmar grunts]

447
00:24:51.865 --> 00:24:53.575
[Bean screaming]

448
00:24:57.121 --> 00:24:58.872
Mom. what did you do that for?

449
00:24:58.956 --> 00:25:02.001
It was the only way to get you
to stop talking. Now swim for that ship.

450
00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:14.972
Welcome aboard.
Queen Dagmar and Princess Tiabeanie.

451
00:25:15.055 --> 00:25:18.684
Mom. what are these creatures.
and why are they looking at me that way?

452
00:25:18.767 --> 00:25:23.439
Bean. you have so much to learn
and many wonderful things to see.

453
00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:27.317
Set sail!
For the homeland and a glorious future!

454
00:25:44.418 --> 00:25:45.753
[sighs]

455
00:25:45.961 --> 00:25:50.549
I guess the only bright side is.
now I got nothing left to lose.

456
00:25:50.966 --> 00:25:52.509
[groans]

457
00:25:52.593 --> 00:25:53.761
[splash]

458
00:25:53.844 --> 00:25:57.347
Except the thing that says I'm a king!

459
00:25:57.514 --> 00:26:00.184
Ah. come on!

460
00:26:00.267 --> 00:26:02.269
[theme music playing]

461
00:26:03.305 --> 00:27:03.243
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today
